      "Explanation": "To eat rice is to take an ordinary meal; Chan records repeatedly use the action in direct answers and in formulas pairing eating with dressing, sleeping, or daily work. The word remains ordinary eating. Zen bends it by putting the unexceptional act into public answers and tests, without making every meal a metaphor."
